net-4-6 as evaluator and user simulator; these are publisher measurements. The run manifests record an Ubuntu 1920x1080 VM on AWS, screenshot observations, the pyautogui action space, benchmark release osworld-v2-2026.06.24 and a separate grounding model (simular-ui-venus-15-30b-a3b-rtx6000). Each run root's manifest describes its last partial invocation (a one-task backfill for run1, a three-task infrastructure rerun for run2). Superseded attempt directories are kept beside the canonical three-digit task directories. The card names a RUNS.md index that is absent at this revision. The Hub license is `other` with no license text.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/simular-ai/sai-osworld-v2-benchmark-runs/raw/fb621da25cb55a45e19f4258eea4c4fd795c625a/README.md","target_id":"organization:simular","type":"published_by"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Simular's per-task evidence from two complete 108-task OSWorld-V2 runs of its Sai computer-use agent: scores, step trajectories, message traces, evaluator and API logs, and run manifests, without screenshots.","task_classes":["R04.03.01.01","R06.02.01.02","R11.01.01.01"],"topics":["evaluation","observability"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/simular-ai/sai-osworld-v2-benchmark-runs"}
